body:
@aymeric-giraudet Thank you so much for the effort to fix this issue 👏

Just one little thing I see when we tested this in our code base (the problem might as well be at our end, but I don't quite see why 🤔 ). To be able to better see what's going on, we have added a console.log to `onStateChange` to the InstantSearch. Like this:

```
const onStateChange = (params: any) => {
  console.log("Query", params.uiState.Data_Set_Test?.query)
  params.setUiState(params.uiState)
}

   <InstantSearch
        searchClient={isServerRendered ? searchClientServer : searchClient}
        indexName="Data_Set_Test"
        onStateChange={onStateChange}
        routing={{ router: createInstantSearchNextRouter({ serverUrl }) }}
      >
```

My Hit component is a link to a detail view. When I go back and forth between the search view and the detail view to verify that the browser back issue is now gone, I notice this in the console. Seems like the console.log statement is printed one more time for each back and forth? Might indicate that something is not cleaned up?
